(cherry picked from commit e1ac1f641ab15b3594ca1752b14f9add55040243)

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y): prerequisite for "[parser] Restore
parse restriction when reparsing Function constructor top-level", which
needs Script::CompilationKind::kFunctionConstructor. On V8 14.8 the Script
flags are still Torque-generated (DEFINE_TORQUE_GENERATED_SCRIPT_FLAGS from
script.tq), so the script.tq change (compilation_kind: 3 bits replacing
compilation_type, plus outer_language_mode) provides the CompilationKindBits
/ OuterLanguageModeBit used by the new accessors, and the hand-written
BitField definitions and accessor declarations upstream added to script.h
are not. Only the CompilationKind enum, its ToString() overload, the
compilation_kind()/outer_language_mode() accessors (with compilation_type()
derived from the kind) and the compiler.cc / parse-info.cc recording hunks
are applied; 14.8 never calls set_compilation_type() elsewhere.

